{"html":"<p>The first Roman emperor, who ruled from 27 BCE until his death in 14 CE. Born Gaius Octavius, he is also called Octavian.</p><p>He was the great-nephew of <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"julius-caesar\">Julius Caesar</a>, who adopted him in his will. At nineteen he raised an army, joined Antony and Lepidus in the <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"second-triumvirate\">Second Triumvirate</a>, and destroyed his enemies. With his friend <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"agrippa\">Agrippa</a> in command he beat Antony and Cleopatra at <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"battle-of-actium\">Actium</a> in 31 BCE.</p><p>In 27 BCE he took the name Augustus (see <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"augustus-becomes-first-emperor\">Augustus becomes first emperor</a>). He kept the outward forms of the Republic but held the armies and the real power. His long reign brought the <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"pax-romana\">Pax Romana</a>, two centuries of relative peace. He said he found Rome a city of brick and left it one of marble, and he built himself the <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"mausoleum-of-augustus\">Mausoleum of Augustus</a>.</p><p>He pushed the frontiers to the Danube and added Egypt, but the loss of three legions at the <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest\">Teutoburg Forest</a> in 9 CE stopped him at the Rhine. His wife <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"livia\">Livia</a> advised him for over fifty years, and her son <a class=\"kbl\" data-k=\"tiberius\">Tiberius</a> succeeded him.</p>","links":["julius-caesar","second-triumvirate","agrippa","battle-of-actium","augustus-becomes-first-emperor","pax-romana","mausoleum-of-augustus","battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest","livia","tiberius"],"sum":"The first Roman emperor, who ruled from 27 BCE until his death in 14 CE. Born Gaius Octavius, he is also called Octavian.","rel":{"where":["roman-empire"]},"back":["aeneid","agrippa","agrippina-the-younger","apollonia-illyria","ara-pacis","assassination-of-julius-caesar","augustus-becomes-first-emperor","augustus